DGR-07: dgraphBand2Ptop()/dgraphGrow2Ptop() free the caller's base-adjusted index array; no NULL guard (status: still-present in 7.0.17, fixed by patch 0001 + 0002)
All reproducers use the shared driver repro/common/g21fi.c and the LD_PRELOAD fault shim repro/common/fishim.c (from G18).
Trees: $WORK/pristinefi = v7.0.17, $WORK/basefi = combined series (base), $WORK/buildfi = base + this series; all built
with CFLAGS "-O0 -g -fsanitize=undefined -ftrivial-auto-var-init=pattern" (ASan cannot be preloaded), see repro/common/build.sh.
  cd $WORK/repro/common && ./build.sh $WORK/pristinefi && ./build.sh $WORK/basefi && ./build.sh $WORK/buildfi
  ./scan.sh LIBDIR BIN NP FAILRANK NTH_FROM NTH_TO -- MODE TOPO BASE NL [ARGS]   (one line per failed allocation index; HANG = 15 s timeout)
Full scan outputs: repro/common/scans/pri_* (v7.0.17), base_* (combined base), fix1_*/fix2_* (patched).

Point-to-point variant is selected on the "sparse" topology with np=4 (only ranks 0 and 1 share an edge).
  ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/g21fi 4 1 3 4 -- band sparse 1 4 2
    nth=3 exit=139 :: SCOTCH_dgraphBand: out of memory (1); dgraph_band_grow.c:439:3: runtime error: store to null pointer (Ptop has no NULL guard)
    nth=4 exit=134 :: dgraphBand2Ptop: out of memory (1); signal 6 (free() of the base-adjusted caller array, then the caller frees it again)
  ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/g21fi 4 1 3 3 -- grow sparse 1 4 3
    nth=3 exit=134 :: dgraphGrow2Ptop: out of memory (1); signal 6 (the USER's partgsttab was freed by the library; the driver's free() aborts)
Patched (buildfi): every rank returns 1, no sanitizer output:
  ./scan.sh $WORK/buildfi/lib ./bin_buildfi/g21fi 4 1 3 4 -- band sparse 1 4 2      -> nth=3,4: rank 0..3: band rc=1
  ./scan.sh $WORK/buildfi/lib ./bin_buildfi/g21fi 4 1 3 3 -- grow sparse 1 4 3      -> nth=3: rank 0..3: grow rc=1
(base-combined behaves like pristine: scans/base_band_sparse_b1.txt, scans/base_grow_sparse_b1.txt)
